# TRAP BAR DEADLIFT

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Trap Bar Deadlift is a bilateral compound exercise designed to develop whole-body force production through simultaneous hip and knee extension.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the most versatile exercises for improving maximal strength, explosive power and athletic performance while reducing spinal stress compared with conventional deadlifts.

---

# Philosophy

The Trap Bar Deadlift combines the advantages of a squat and a deadlift.

Its neutral grip, centered load and upright posture allow athletes to produce high levels of force with excellent movement efficiency.

CAS frequently prioritizes this exercise when the objective is maximizing athletic transfer while minimizing unnecessary mechanical stress.

